  "verdict": "The double-sealed M2057 canonical population independently reproduces all 1920 fixed post-load VCS component workloads. Its 1917 inherited logs are byte-identical to the valid M2053 raw logs and its three successor logs are byte-identical to the M2057 raw runs for slots 86, 893, and 1755, all using the exact inherited compiled simv. M2053 remains FAILED_OR_INCOMPLETE_DO_NOT_CITE; the composite is legal only when disclosed as a 1917+3 same-image cross-attempt result, never as one successful M2053 attempt or an automatic retry. Independent parsing reproduces 12522876 ordinary-LRU4 cycles versus 5124365 TSBG-B4 cycles, 2.4437907916x weighted component speedup, 59.0799669% post-load time reduction, and 64.2523441% scalar-request reduction. This admits a VCS component table and scoped abstract result for the fixed ep34 real-descriptor population. It does not admit all FC2 layers, full-token/full-FC/full-network/system speedup, real weights, power, energy, same area, or paper PPA.",
